  "fromId": "w",
  "toId": "m",
  "preamble": "The change of the labio-velar approximant [w] to the bilabial nasal [m] happens when [w] stands before a nasal vowel: the velum lowering of the vowel spreads onto the glide, and a nasalized labial closure is heard as [m]. It is attested in Mixtec varieties, where Proto-Mixtec *w became m before nasalized vowels.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Nasalization, Nasal Assimilation",
  "languageExamples": [
